Subject: [PATCH] extensions: pref to stop extensions recolouring the browser

Why Firefox source must change:
  Extensions with the "theme" permission (Dark Reader's "Change browser
  theme", for one) recolour the browser through browser.theme.update(). A
  window with such a theme is a themed window ([lwtheme]): Firefox drops
  the system backdrop for it and Aequera keeps its frame solid, so one
  extension silently replaces the glass frame material with an opaque
  colour (docs/design/MATERIAL.md). Firefox has no pref, policy, or
  permission setting that refuses these updates while keeping the
  extension; the API is implemented in toolkit's ext-theme.js.

What it changes:
  - theme.update() resolves without applying anything while
    aequera.extensions.dynamicThemes is false (Aequera's default,
    aequera-prefs.js), and emits theme.onUpdated with the theme actually
    in use, so listeners stay in sync with theme.getCurrent(). The
    extension keeps running and sees success. A window ID is still
    validated as upstream does, so an invalid one is still refused.
  - Static themes (theme add-ons, the Themes tab) are a separate path
    (onManifestEntry) and are unaffected; so are theme.reset() and its
    onUpdated emissions.
  - The pref is absent in Firefox and defaults to true here, so with
    Firefox's defaults nothing changes. Turning it on lets extensions
    recolour again from their next update; turning it off leaves a theme
    already applied in place until it is reset or the browser restarts.

Depends on: nothing.
Validation: aequera/shell/firefox/tests/browser/browser_aequera_extension_themes.js
  (a "theme"-permission extension cannot recolour the window or end the
  glass frame by default, and is told the theme in use; with the pref on
  its theme applies); Firefox's browser_ext_themes_dynamic_*.js,
  _reset.js, and _static_onUpdated.js with Firefox's defaults
  (tools/build/test-shell.sh upstream).
Upstream risk: low; one guard and an event emission in a small, stable
  API method.

diff --git a/toolkit/components/extensions/parent/ext-theme.js b/toolkit/components/extensions/parent/ext-theme.js
index f6ea1ff9521f..a9134d4ac686 100644
--- a/toolkit/components/extensions/parent/ext-theme.js
+++ b/toolkit/components/extensions/parent/ext-theme.js
@@ -248,6 +248,28 @@ this.theme = class extends ExtensionAPIPersistent {
             }
           }
 
+          if (
+            !Services.prefs.getBoolPref(
+              "aequera.extensions.dynamicThemes",
+              true
+            )
+          ) {
+            // The call resolves, changes nothing, and reports the theme in
+            // use, as a successful update would: theme.onUpdated listeners
+            // stay in sync with theme.getCurrent().
+            const browserWindow = windowId
+              ? windowTracker.getWindow(windowId, context)
+              : null;
+            onUpdatedEmitter.emit(
+              "theme-updated",
+              browserWindow && windowOverrides.has(browserWindow)
+                ? windowOverrides.get(browserWindow).details
+                : defaultTheme.details,
+              windowId
+            );
+            return Promise.resolve();
+          }
+
           new Theme({
             extension,
             details,
